{title: Say Amen}
{key: C}

{comment: Intro}
[Cm]      [Abmaj7]         [Fm7]       [Bbsus]

{comment: Verse 1}
[Eb]We're all on a journey and we're [Fm7]called to walk by [Eb]faith
And there will always be the mountains and [Cm]valleys in our way
But [Abmaj7]right here in this [Bb]moment may our [Ab]strength be [Eb/G]renewed
As [Ab]we recall what [Eb/G]God has done and [Bbsus]how we've seen him [Bbsus]move

{comment: Chorus}
If there's [Abmaj7]anybody here who's found him faithful
[Fm7]Anybody here who knows he's [Eb]able
[Ab]Say  [Eb]amen
And if there's [Abmaj7]anybody here who's seen his power
[Fm7]Anybody here brought through the [Eb]fire
[Ab]Say  [Eb]amen
Anybody [Abmaj7]here found joy in the [Eb/G]midst of sorrow
[Abmaj7]Peace in the storm and [Eb/G]hope for tomor[Abmaj7]row
And you've seen it [Eb/G]time and time a[Ab]gain
Just [Ab/Bb]say amen[Cm7][Bb][Abmaj7][Ab/Bb]

{comment: Verse 2}
[Eb]Sometimes through the darkness [Fm7]it gets hard to [Eb]see
But [Eb]be bold and courages and [Ab]follow where he [Cm]leads
'cause [Abmaj7]greater is the one who's [Bb]in us than [Ab]he who's in the [Eb]world
So [Ab]child of God re[Eb/G]member the [Bbsus]battle is the Lord's

{comment: Bridge}
Just [Abmaj7]stand and [Eb/G]testify
Of the [Abmaj7]greatness of God in our [Bbsus]lives
{ci: Raise Key Whole Step}
